<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="CH2b1559-en-18cfe757" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Draft translation of 聲無哀樂論</title><editor role="translator">Christoph Harbsmeier</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title>Draft translation of 聲無哀樂論</title>Draft: Oxford, 1971</bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#CH2b1559"><title xml:lang="och"/></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2026-05-10T21:05:56.502+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="CH2b1559-start"><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.59" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:22:36.701+09:00">So then: the Music says this; the Music says that,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.60" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:32:04.919+09:00">is there no more to it than bells and drums (and no more)? [Music is more than the bells and drums that express it.]</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.61" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:23:53.965+09:00">Grief speaks of this, Grief speaks of that,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.62" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:32:53.359+09:00">is there no more to it than wailing and weeping? [Grief is more than its expression in wailing and weeping!</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.63" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:36:28.282+09:00">Speaking along these lines</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.64" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:37:49.348+09:00">jade and silk are not the substance of ritual (and?) deference</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.65" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:44:26.518+09:00">song and dance performance is not the main point of mourning.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.66" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:45:06.742+09:00">How is one to make all this plain?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.67" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:46:22.444+09:00">So: different regions have different customs:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.68" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:48:18.979+09:00">their chanting and wailing is not the same.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.69" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:02:51.617+09:00">When used in complex contexts</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.70" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:03:14.87+09:00">some will hear wailing and feel elated,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.71" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:11:02.719+09:00">others will hear singing and feel dejected,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.72" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:12:02.008+09:00">and yet their feelings of grief and joy are quite the same.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.73" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:12:30.414+09:00">Now if on the basis of quite the same feelings</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.74" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:13:07.62+09:00">one emits vastly different sounds,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.75" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:15:28.515+09:00">is this not because the sound of music is not emotionally constant?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.76" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:24:06.405+09:00">And yet the harmonious juxtaposition of musical tones</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.77" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:24:49.819+09:00">is what affects humans most profoundly.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.78" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:26:39.863+09:00">toiling workers sing songs to their work,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.79" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:29:51.532+09:00">those pleased with themselves celebrate their feats through dances.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.80" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:31:53.835+09:00">And so those who suffer sad pain in their hearts</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.81" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:34:28.541+09:00">will come up with acutely sorrowful words.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.82" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:35:15.87+09:00">Words properly aligned become songs,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.83" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:36:11.125+09:00">sounds properly aligned become music:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.84" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:38:11.79+09:00">one mixes these together to intone them,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.85" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:38:29.503+09:00">and one gathers to listen to them.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.86" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:39:27.144+09:00">The mind gets moved by sounds in harmony,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.87" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:42:10.388+09:00">and empathy is aroused by bitter words:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.88" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:43:21.463+09:00">but before the sighs grow still</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.89" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:44:55.471+09:00">the tears are cascading.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.90" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:45:23.446+09:00">The mourning heart stays hidden inside,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.91" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:49:05.708+09:00">only when exposed to harmonious musical cadence it comes to light. </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.92" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-13T23:10:27.333+09:00">The harmonious musical cadence has no  one (fixed/determinate) symbolic form (harmonious cadence can by formed between any tones, not only one certain pattern待考),</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.93" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-13T23:11:36.36+09:00">whereas the mournful heart has one (fixed/determinant) dominant mode.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.94" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-13T23:08:06.786+09:00">So then, with a mournful heart belonging to one fixed mode</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.95" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-13T23:13:19.661+09:00">on the occasion of a harmonious musical cadence that has no fixed symbolic form</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.96" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:58:55.731+09:00">what one is struck by</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.97" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:18:29.856+09:00">is only mournful grief, that is all:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.98" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:21:28.756+09:00">they no longer have any idea of Zhuang Zhou's "the blowing (in the cosmic cavities) being different in myriads of ways</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.99" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:22:04.793+09:00">and of it causing itself to cease"!</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.100" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:25:11.014+09:00">As customs and manners take their course</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.101" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:58:31.833+09:00">these end up shaping (political) administrations.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.102" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:52:10.989+09:00">on the basis of this the histories of the states elucidate the successes and failures of administration and education</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.103" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:59:14.133+09:00">investigate the thriving and the decline of the local music of the states, </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.104" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T23:02:16.055+09:00">and sing the songs of men's natural feelings and their basic nature</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.105" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:57:30.893+09:00">thus implicitly offering critical encouragements to the rulership.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.106" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T23:03:39.051+09:00">Therefore it says (in the 詩序):</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.107" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T23:06:45.233+09:00">"The music of a doomed state is mournful and then wistful."</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-7a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-14T19:34:12.478+09:00">4.2 </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.77" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T21:39:39.916+09:00">making one agitated or serene,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.78" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T21:42:07.951+09:00">that is the extrinsic effect of the sounds of music.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:29:43.672+09:00">Thus the mind is bound by a host of concerns,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:29:49.038+09:00">but the Five Notes are in concert,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:32:04.511+09:00">and therefore one feels pleasantly relaxed and satisfied.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:33:58.731+09:00">And in this way all the notes are essentially simple, complex, high, low, well executed or badly,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:36:48.348+09:00">and the human sensibilities respond with agitation or serenity, concentrated focus or dissolution.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.44" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:43:43.407+09:00">Just as when you wander about in the markets of the capitals</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:48:41.008+09:00">then one's eyes get overexcited and one's urged run wild:  </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:49:21.207+09:00">but when one settles down to observing the measures of music</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:50:04.779+09:00">then one's thoughts are serene and one's face is straight.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:51:28.237+09:00">This is because the essence of musical melody</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:52:35.769+09:00">is all in relaxation and stressfulness.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.50" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:53:21.908+09:00">The emotional response to musical sound</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T23:14:20.836+09:00">is limited to agitation and serenity."</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:09:12.588+09:00">the musical notes of a well-governed age are serene so as to induce joy,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:26:11.869+09:00">and the musical noted of  a doomed age are mournful so as to induce wistfulness. </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:10:15.01+09:00">Now generally, good government and political chaos depend on governance,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:14:08.294+09:00">and the sound of the musical notes then reflect (the contrasting kinds of governance).</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T20:48:03.394+09:00">So, then, the emotions of grief and wistfulness</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:14:34.173+09:00">are expressed by metal and stone (musical instruments),</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:14:46.72+09:00">and the abstract feature of of serenity and joy</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:19:16.859+09:00">takes shape through wind and string instruments.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:20:55.914+09:00">And there again, when Zhongni came to hear the "Shao" music</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:28:05.356+09:00">he recognised in it the virtue of Shun;</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:28:54.75+09:00">and when Ji Zha listened to the string music</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:29:30.301+09:00">he got to understand the customs of all the states.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:29:49.481+09:00">These are established facts of the past,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:36:33.534+09:00">and the great worthies of former times had no doubts about them.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:33:57.499+09:00">Now just you alone have this idea that there is no emotion like grief and joy in the the sounds (of music).</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:34:26.827+09:00">Where on earth are your arguments?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:39:34.751+09:00">If you have terrific investigations to report</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:41:20.15+09:00">please let us have the explanations without delay!</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:42:06.343+09:00">The Host responded as follows:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:51:29.103+09:00">"On this issue people have long been stuck:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:55:55.947+09:00">no one has it in him to sort this out.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:58:24.064+09:00">That's what got us to the stage, through the ages,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:01:36.353+09:00">people have been all wrong about the ins and outs of this.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:05:23.654+09:00">So, without delay , having gratefully received your guidance</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:53:34.294+09:00">I shall go ahead put in words at least one corner of all this.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:07:33.445+09:00">There was a Stranger from Qin who consulted the Host of the Eastern Wilds as follows:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:08:22.49+09:00">I'm told that past opinion holds it that</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:54:48.379+09:00">So then: When the two vital energies of Heaven and Earth commerge</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:55:37.16+09:00">then all manner of creatures get to be born and to grow, </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:58:44.174+09:00">the cold and the hot seasons get to take their turns</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:01:14.778+09:00">and the Five Agents take their full forms.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:05:41.903+09:00">they become visible with the five colours (the world of colours),</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:06:20.189+09:00">and they emit the fives tones (the world of sounds).</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:07:22.952+09:00">The emergence of tones and sounds (of music)</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:13:33.843+09:00">is perhaps like the existence of smells and flavours between Heaven and Earth:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:19:35.607+09:00">No matter how excellent or otherwise</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:19:45.115+09:00">and even after they have been exposed to dirty contamination,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:23:58.565+09:00">their essential substance remains the natural same</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:24:42.29+09:00">and it does not fundamentally change.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:26:54.443+09:00">How could the handling of these things in terms of preference or aversion</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:30:40.554+09:00">and how indeed could emotions like grief and joy change one's objective assessment of these things?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.44" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:33:56.492+09:00">So when it comes to the tones like gong and shang, when they are gathered and juxtaposed</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:36:26.094+09:00">that then the musical tones be in striking harmony</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:44:48.332+09:00">that effect is the utmost hope for the human mind</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:49:44.977+09:00">it is what one's essential desires are smitten by.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:50:16.821+09:00">The ancients understood that emotions must not be indulgent,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:51:09.647+09:00">that desires must not be extreme,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.50" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:52:12.625+09:00">and so as circumstances require</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:53:40.919+09:00">one moderates every on of these emotions and desires,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.52" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:57:36.45+09:00">one sees to it that grief does not get to the stage of desolation</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.53" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:00:45.568+09:00">and that joy does not reach the stage of euphoria,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.54" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:07:59.023+09:00">For practical reasons one gives names to things,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.55" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:08:42.039+09:00">and so things have their appellations.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.56" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:10:47.434+09:00">When someone weeps one diagnoses grief,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.57" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:11:05.849+09:00">when someone sings one diagnoses joy.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.108" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:27:29.476+09:00">Happiness, anger, mournfulness and joy,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.109" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:27:46.35+09:00">love, hatred, shame and fear:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.110" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:30:44.731+09:00">Quite generally, it is by these eight</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.111" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:33:52.813+09:00">that living humans relate to things and transmit their emotions.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.112" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:34:07.734+09:00">Each of these eight belongs to its distinct kind</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.113" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:36:09.745+09:00">and they must not be confounded.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.114" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:43:20.13+09:00">Now, flavours are called (things like) sweet or bitter;</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.117" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:48:35.371+09:00">then the love and hate are properly be predicated me</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.115" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:45:39.907+09:00">If, for example, because X is talented and I like him subjectively,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.116" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:46:47.104+09:00">and because B is stupid and I emotionally dislike him,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.118" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:55:20.948+09:00">whereas talent and stupidity are properly predicated of A and B (respectively).</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.119" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:59:23.804+09:00">For can one, just because one loves a person predicate of him that he loves others?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.120" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T05:04:00.307+09:00">And can one, just because I hate a person say of him that he "hates others"?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.121" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T05:09:22.606+09:00">something one prefers, does one say of that that it "prefers the taste"?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.122" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T05:12:43.886+09:00">something one finds tastes awful, does one say of that that it finds the taste awful?</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>